        "content": "     1→[\n     2→  {\n     3→    \"title\": \"The US is winning the AI race in commercialization\",\n     4→    \"description\": \"Analysis arguing that the US is winning the AI race where it matters most: commercialization and practical application of AI technologies, rather than just research breakthroughs.\",\n     5→    \"author\": \"Hacker News community\",\n     6→    \"source\": \"Hacker News\",\n     7→    \"url\": \"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=40823421\",\n     8→    \"published_date\": \"2026-05-14\",\n     9→    \"topics\": [\"ai\", \"commercialization\", \"us-china\", \"ai-strategy\", \"market-dynamics\"],\n    10→    \"type\": \"discussion\"\n    11→  },\n    12→  {\n    13→    \"title\": \"Notion turns workspace into AI agent hub\",\n    14→    \"description\": \"Notion launched a developer platform that transforms its workspace into a hub for AI agents, allowing developers to build and integrate AI agents directly into Notion workspaces.\",\n    15→    \"author\": \"Sarah Perez\",\n    16→    \"source\": \"Tech Media\",\n    17→    \"url\": \"https://techcrunch.com/2026/05/13/notion-ai-agent-platform/\",\n    18→    \"published_date\": \"2026-05-13\",\n    19→    \"topics\": [\"ai\", \"ai-agents\", \"notion\", \"developer-platform\", \"productivity\"],\n    20→    \"type\": \"news\"\n    21→  },\n    22→  {\n    23→    \"title\": \"AI voice startup Vapi hits $500M valuation\",\n    24→    \"description\": \"AI voice startup Vapi reached a $500M valuation after winning Amazon Ring as a customer over 40 competitors. Their AI voice technology is being adopted for customer service and voice applications.\",\n    25→    \"author\": \"Jagmeet Singh\",\n    26→    \"source\": \"Tech Media\",\n    27→    \"url\": \"https://techcrunch.com/2026/05/13/vapi-voice-ai-valuation/\",\n    28→    \"published_date\": \"2026-05-13\",\n    29→    \"topics\": [\"ai\", \"voice-ai\", \"startups\", \"amazon\", \"valuation\"],\n    30→    \"type\": \"news\"\n    31→  },\n    32→  {\n    33→    \"title\": \"Adaption aims big with AutoScientist\",\n    34→    \"description\": \"Adaption announced AutoScientist, an AI tool designed to help models train themselves, representing advances in self-improving AI systems and automated research capabilities.\",\n    35→    \"author\": \"Russell Brandom\",\n    36→    \"source\": \"Tech Media\",\n    37→    \"url\": \"https://techcrunch.com/2026/05/13/adaption-autoscientist-ai/\",\n    38→    \"published_date\": \"2026-05-13\",\n    39→    \"topics\": [\"ai\", \"auto-ml\", \"self-improving-ai\", \"research-tools\"],\n    40→    \"type\": \"news\"\n    41→  },\n    42→  {\n    43→    \"title\": \"Anthropic Cat Wu on AI anticipating user needs\",\n    44→    \"description\": \"Anthropic's Cat Wu discussed the future of AI systems that can anticipate user needs before users themselves know what they are, representing a shift toward proactive AI assistance.\",\n    45→    \"author\": \"Lucas Ropek\",\n    46→    \"source\": \"Tech Media\",\n    47→    \"url\": \"https://techcrunch.com/2026/05/13/anthropic-cat-wu-interview/\",\n    48→    \"published_date\": \"2026-05-13\",\n    49→    \"topics\": [\"anthropic\", \"claude\", \"ai\", \"proactive-ai\", \"user-experience\"],\n    50→    \"type\": \"interview\"\n    51→  },\n    52→  {\n    53→    \"title\": \"Leaving GitHub for Forgejo\",\n    54→    \"description\": \"Developer discusses reasons for leaving GitHub for Forgejo, a self-hosted Git forge. Raises questions about platform lock-in, open source alternatives, and developer tool choices in the AI era.\",\n    55→    \"author\": \"jorijn\",\n    56→    \"source\": \"Hacker News\",\n    57→    \"url\": \"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=40812345\",\n    58→    \"published_date\": \"2026-05-13\",\n    59→    \"topics\": [\"github\", \"forgejo\", \"git-hosting\", \"open-source\", \"platform-alternatives\"],\n    60→    \"type\": \"discussion\"\n    61→  },\n    62→  {\n    63→    \"title\": \"GM lays off IT workers to hire AI specialists\",\n    64→    \"description\": \"General Motors laid off hundreds of IT workers to hire employees with stronger AI skills, reflecting a broader trend of companies restructuring their technical workforce to focus on AI capabilities.\",\n    65→    \"author\": \"Kirsten Korosec\",\n    66→    \"source\": \"Tech Media\",\n    67→    \"url\": \"https://techcrunch.com/2026/05/12/gm-layoffs-it-ai-skills/\",\n    68→    \"published_date\": \"2026-05-12\",\n    69→    \"topics\": [\"ai\", \"workforce\", \"hiring\", \"corporate-strategy\", \"it-jobs\"],\n    70→    \"type\": \"news\"\n    71→  },\n    72→  {\n    73→    \"title\": \"Google brings agentic AI and vibe-coded widgets to Android\",\n    74→    \"description\": \"Google announced agentic AI capabilities and 'vibe-coded' widgets for Android, allowing users to create widgets through natural language prompts. The 'Create My Widget' feature enables anyone to generate custom widgets without coding.\",\n    75→    \"author\": \"Ivan Mehta\",\n    76→    \"source\": \"Tech Media\",\n    77→    \"url\": \"https://techcrunch.com/2026/05/12/google-android-agentic-ai-widgets/\",\n    78→    \"published_date\": \"2026-05-12\",\n    79→    \"topics\": [\"google\", \"android\", \"agentic-ai\", \"vibe-coding\", \"low-code\", \"widgets\"],\n    80→    \"type\": \"news\"\n    81→  },\n    82→  {\n    83→    \"title\": \"Digg relaunches as AI news aggregator\",\n    84→    \"description\": \"Social news pioneer Digg relaunched as an AI-powered news aggregator, attempting to reinvent itself for the AI era by using algorithms to curate and summarize news content.\",\n    85→    \"author\": \"Sarah Perez\",\n    86→    \"source\": \"Tech Media\",\n    87→    \"url\": \"https://techcrunch.com/2026/05/12/digg-ai-news-aggregator/\",\n    88→    \"published_date\": \"2026-05-12\",\n    89→    \"topics\": [\"ai\", \"news-aggregation\", \"digg\", \"media\", \"summarization\"],\n    90→    \"type\": \"news\"\n    91→  },\n    92→  {\n    93→    \"title\": \"The Changelog: Amelia Wattenberger on Intent and agent-first design\",\n    94→    \"description\": \"Interview with designer Amelia Wattenberger about Intent at Augment Code. Discussion on the identity crisis developers face as agents take over, the redesign of developer tooling for agent-first workflows, and the evolution from autocomplete to chat to UI. Key insight: prototyping got easier but finishing got harder.\",\n    95→    \"author\": \"The Changelog\",\n    96→    \"source\": \"Podcast\",\n    97→    \"url\": \"https://changelog.com/podcast/608\",\n    98→    \"published_date\": \"2026-05-12\",\n    99→    \"topics\": [\"ai\", \"coding\", \"developer-tools\", \"agentic-ai\", \"design\", \"intent\"],\n   100→    \"type\": \"podcast\"\n   101→  },\n   102→  {\n   103→    \"title\": \"Googlebooks and vibe-coded widgets announced at Android Show\",\n   104→    \"description\": \"Google announced Googlebooks and vibe-coded widgets at their Android Show event, showcasing the company's push toward AI-generated and customizable widget creation for Android users.\",\n   105→    \"author\": \"Sarah Perez, Ivan Mehta, Aisha Malik\",\n   106→    \"source\": \"Tech Media\",\n   107→    \"url\": \"https://techcrunch.com/2026/05/11/google-android-show-announcements/\",\n   108→    \"published_date\": \"2026-05-11\",\n   109→    \"topics\": [\"google\", \"android\", \"vibe-coding\", \"widgets\", \"ai-generated-content\"],\n   110→    \"type\": \"news\"\n   111→  },\n   112→  {\n   113→    \"title\": \"The Changelog: Astral joins OpenAI\",\n   114→    \"description\": \"Discussion about Astral joining OpenAI and what this signals about the center of gravity moving for developer tools. Also covered: LiteLLM supply-chain attack, OpenCode as an open-source coding-agent stack, Rust's reality check on pain points, and WorkOS pushing AuthKit into CLI auth.\",\n   115→    \"author\": \"The Changelog\",\n   116→    \"source\": \"Podcast\",\n   117→    \"url\": \"https://changelog.com/podcast/607\",\n   118→    \"published_date\": \"2026-05-10\",\n   119→    \"topics\": [\"openai\", \"astral\", \"developer-tools\", \"supply-chain-security\", \"rust\", \"cli-auth\"],\n   120→    \"type\": \"podcast\"\n   121→  },\n   122→  {\n   123→    \"title\": \"A History of IDEs at Google\",\n   124→    \"description\": \"Detailed discussion about the evolution of Integrated Development Environments used internally at Google, providing insights into how a major tech company approaches developer tooling.\",\n   125→    \"author\": \"laurentlb\",\n   126→    \"source\": \"Hacker News\",\n   127→    \"url\": \"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=40789234\",\n   128→    \"published_date\": \"2026-05-10\",\n   129→    \"topics\": [\"google\", \"ides\", \"developer-tools\", \"engineering-culture\", \"tooling\"],\n   130→    \"type\": \"discussion\"\n   131→  },\n   132→  {\n   133→    \"title\": \"The Changelog: Tailscale's TSIDP, TSNet, and Aperture\",\n   134→    \"description\": \"Interview with Tailscale co-founder David Carney about TSIDP (clickless auth), TSNet apps, multiple tailnets for isolation, and Aperture - Tailscale's private AI gateway for API key management, observability, and agent security.\",\n   135→    \"author\": \"The Changelog\",\n   136→    \"source\": \"Podcast\",\n   137→    \"url\": \"https://changelog.com/podcast/606\",\n   138→    \"published_date\": \"2026-05-09\",\n   139→    \"topics\": [\"tailscale\", \"infrastructure\", \"auth\", \"ai-gateway\", \"security\", \"observability\"],\n   140→    \"type\": \"podcast\"\n   141→  },\n   142→  {\n   143→    \"title\": \"The Changelog: Iran bombed AWS, OpenAI GPT-5.4, living brain cells play DOOM\",\n   144→    \"description\": \"Discussion of major AI news: Iran allegedly bombed AWS data centers to take down Claude, OpenAI released GPT-5.4 with significant coding improvements, and living brain cells were taught to play DOOM. Also covered: new MacBook Pros with M5 Pro/Max.\",\n   145→    \"author\": \"The Changelog\",\n   146→    \"source\": \"Podcast\",\n   147→    \"url\": \"https://changelog.com/podcast/605\",\n   148→    \"published_date\": \"2026-05-08\",\n   149→    \"topics\": [\"openai\", \"gpt-5.4\", \"anthropic\", \"claude\", \"aws\", \"infrastructure\", \"brain-computer-interface\"],\n   150→    \"type\": \"podcast\"\n   151→  },\n   152→  {\n   153→    \"title\": \"The Changelog: Burke Holland on Opus 4.5 and AI coding\",\n   154→    \"description\": \"Burke Holland from GitHub Copilot discusses how Opus 4.5 changed everything in AI coding, the 2x usage bump from Claude, and GPT-5.3 Codex living up to the hype. Deep dive into practical AI coding workflows.\",\n   155→    \"author\": \"The Changelog\",\n   156→    \"source\": \"Podcast\",\n   157→    \"url\": \"https://changelog.com/podcast/604\",\n   158→    \"published_date\": \"2026-05-08\",\n   159→    \"topics\": [\"ai\", \"coding\", \"github-copilot\", \"anthropic\", \"claude\", \"openai\", \"gpt-5.3\", \"gpt-5.4\", \"developer-experience\"],\n   160→    \"type\": \"podcast\"\n   161→  },\n   162→  {\n   163→    \"title\": \"Using Claude Code: The Unreasonable Effectiveness of HTML\",\n   164→    \"description\": \"Thariq Shihipar (Claude Code team) advocates for HTML over Markdown as LLM output format. HTML enables SVG diagrams, interactive widgets, in-page navigation, and richer explanations. Simon tested this by having GPT-5.5 create an HTML explanation of the copy.fail Linux security exploit, producing rich, interactive documentation.\",\n   165→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison (citing Thariq Shihipar)\",\n   166→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   167→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/May/8/html/\",\n   168→    \"published_date\": \"2026-05-08\",\n   169→    \"topics\": [\"llm\", \"prompt-engineering\", \"html\", \"claude-code\", \"documentation\"],\n   170→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   171→  }\n   172→]\n   173→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"
      }
    ]
