      "content": "[\n  {\n    \"title\": \"The US is winning the AI race in commercialization\",\n    \"description\": \"Analysis arguing that the US is winning the AI race where it matters most: commercialization and practical application of AI technologies, rather than just research breakthroughs.\",\n    \"author\": \"Hacker News community\",\n    \"source\": \"Hacker News\",\n    \"url\": \"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=40823421\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-05-14\",\n    \"topics\": [\"ai\", \"commercialization\", \"us-china\", \"ai-strategy\", \"market-dynamics\"],\n    \"type\": \"discussion\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"Notion turns workspace into AI agent hub\",\n    \"description\": \"Notion launched a developer platform that transforms its workspace into a hub for AI agents, allowing developers to build and integrate AI agents directly into Notion workspaces.\",\n    \"author\": \"Sarah Perez\",\n    \"source\": \"Tech Media\",\n    \"url\": \"https://techcrunch.com/2026/05/13/notion-ai-agent-platform/\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-05-13\",\n    \"topics\": [\"ai\", \"ai-agents\", \"notion\", \"developer-platform\", \"productivity\"],\n    \"type\": \"news\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"AI voice startup Vapi hits $500M valuation\",\n    \"description\": \"AI voice startup Vapi reached a $500M valuation after winning Amazon Ring as a customer over 40 competitors. Their AI voice technology is being adopted for customer service and voice applications.\",\n    \"author\": \"Jagmeet Singh\",\n    \"source\": \"Tech Media\",\n    \"url\": \"https://techcrunch.com/2026/05/13/vapi-voice-ai-valuation/\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-05-13\",\n    \"topics\": [\"ai\", \"voice-ai\", \"startups\", \"amazon\", \"valuation\"],\n    \"type\": \"news\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"Adaption aims big with AutoScientist\",\n    \"description\": \"Adaption announced AutoScientist, an AI tool designed to help models train themselves, representing advances in self-improving AI systems and automated research capabilities.\",\n    \"author\": \"Russell Brandom\",\n    \"source\": \"Tech Media\",\n    \"url\": \"https://techcrunch.com/2026/05/13/adaption-autoscientist-ai/\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-05-13\",\n    \"topics\": [\"ai\", \"auto-ml\", \"self-improving-ai\", \"research-tools\"],\n    \"type\": \"news\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"Anthropic Cat Wu on AI anticipating user needs\",\n    \"description\": \"Anthropic's Cat Wu discussed the future of AI systems that can anticipate user needs before users themselves know what they are, representing a shift toward proactive AI assistance.\",\n    \"author\": \"Lucas Ropek\",\n    \"source\": \"Tech Media\",\n    \"url\": \"https://techcrunch.com/2026/05/13/anthropic-cat-wu-interview/\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-05-13\",\n    \"topics\": [\"anthropic\", \"claude\", \"ai\", \"proactive-ai\", \"user-experience\"],\n    \"type\": \"interview\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"Leaving GitHub for Forgejo\",\n    \"description\": \"Developer discusses reasons for leaving GitHub for Forgejo, a self-hosted Git forge. Raises questions about platform lock-in, open source alternatives, and developer tool choices in the AI era.\",\n    \"author\": \"jorijn\",\n    \"source\": \"Hacker News\",\n    \"url\": \"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=40812345\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-05-13\",\n    \"topics\": [\"github\", \"forgejo\", \"git-hosting\", \"open-source\", \"platform-alternatives\"],\n    \"type\": \"discussion\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"GM lays off IT workers to hire AI specialists\",\n    \"description\": \"General Motors laid off hundreds of IT workers to hire employees with stronger AI skills, reflecting a broader trend of companies restructuring their technical workforce to focus on AI capabilities.\",\n    \"author\": \"Kirsten Korosec\",\n    \"source\": \"Tech Media\",\n    \"url\": \"https://techcrunch.com/2026/05/12/gm-layoffs-it-ai-skills/\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-05-12\",\n    \"topics\": [\"ai\", \"workforce\", \"hiring\", \"corporate-strategy\", \"it-jobs\"],\n    \"type\": \"news\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"Google brings agentic AI and vibe-coded widgets to Android\",\n    \"description\": \"Google announced agentic AI capabilities and 'vibe-coded' widgets for Android, allowing users to create widgets through natural language prompts. The 'Create My Widget' feature enables anyone to generate custom widgets without coding.\",\n    \"author\": \"Ivan Mehta\",\n    \"source\": \"Tech Media\",\n    \"url\": \"https://techcrunch.com/2026/05/12/google-android-agentic-ai-widgets/\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-05-12\",\n    \"topics\": [\"google\", \"android\", \"agentic-ai\", \"vibe-coding\", \"low-code\", \"widgets\"],\n    \"type\": \"news\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"Digg relaunches as AI news aggregator\",\n    \"description\": \"Social news pioneer Digg relaunched as an AI-powered news aggregator, attempting to reinvent itself for the AI era by using algorithms to curate and summarize news content.\",\n    \"author\": \"Sarah Perez\",\n    \"source\": \"Tech Media\",\n    \"url\": \"https://techcrunch.com/2026/05/12/digg-ai-news-aggregator/\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-05-12\",\n    \"topics\": [\"ai\", \"news-aggregation\", \"digg\", \"media\", \"summarization\"],\n    \"type\": \"news\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"The Changelog: Amelia Wattenberger on Intent and agent-first design\",\n    \"description\": \"Interview with designer Amelia Wattenberger about Intent at Augment Code. Discussion on the identity crisis developers face as agents take over, the redesign of developer tooling for agent-first workflows, and the evolution from autocomplete to chat to UI. Key insight: prototyping got easier but finishing got harder.\",\n    \"author\": \"The Changelog\",\n    \"source\": \"Podcast\",\n    \"url\": \"https://changelog.com/podcast/608\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-05-12\",\n    \"topics\": [\"ai\", \"coding\", \"developer-tools\", \"agentic-ai\", \"design\", \"intent\"],\n    \"type\": \"podcast\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"Googlebooks and vibe-coded widgets announced at Android Show\",\n    \"description\": \"Google announced Googlebooks and vibe-coded widgets at their Android Show event, showcasing the company's push toward AI-generated and customizable widget creation for Android users.\",\n    \"author\": \"Sarah Perez, Ivan Mehta, Aisha Malik\",\n    \"source\": \"Tech Media\",\n    \"url\": \"https://techcrunch.com/2026/05/11/google-android-show-announcements/\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-05-11\",\n    \"topics\": [\"google\", \"android\", \"vibe-coding\", \"widgets\", \"ai-generated-content\"],\n    \"type\": \"news\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"The Changelog: Astral joins OpenAI\",\n    \"description\": \"Discussion about Astral joining OpenAI and what this signals about the center of gravity moving for developer tools. Also covered: LiteLLM supply-chain attack, OpenCode as an open-source coding-agent stack, Rust's reality check on pain points, and WorkOS pushing AuthKit into CLI auth.\",\n    \"author\": \"The Changelog\",\n    \"source\": \"Podcast\",\n    \"url\": \"https://changelog.com/podcast/607\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-05-10\",\n    \"topics\": [\"openai\", \"astral\", \"developer-tools\", \"supply-chain-security\", \"rust\", \"cli-auth\"],\n    \"type\": \"podcast\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"A History of IDEs at Google\",\n    \"description\": \"Detailed discussion about the evolution of Integrated Development Environments used internally at Google, providing insights into how a major tech company approaches developer tooling.\",\n    \"author\": \"laurentlb\",\n    \"source\": \"Hacker News\",\n    \"url\": \"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=40789234\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-05-10\",\n    \"topics\": [\"google\", \"ides\", \"developer-tools\", \"engineering-culture\", \"tooling\"],\n    \"type\": \"discussion\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"The Changelog: Tailscale's TSIDP, TSNet, and Aperture\",\n    \"description\": \"Interview with Tailscale co-founder David Carney about TSIDP (clickless auth), TSNet apps, multiple tailnets for isolation, and Aperture - Tailscale's private AI gateway for API key management, observability, and agent security.\",\n    \"author\": \"The Changelog\",\n    \"source\": \"Podcast\",\n    \"url\": \"https://changelog.com/podcast/606\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-05-09\",\n    \"topics\": [\"tailscale\", \"infrastructure\", \"auth\", \"ai-gateway\", \"security\", \"observability\"],\n    \"type\": \"podcast\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"The Changelog: Iran bombed AWS, OpenAI GPT-5.4, living brain cells play DOOM\",\n    \"description\": \"Discussion of major AI news: Iran allegedly bombed AWS data centers to take down Claude, OpenAI released GPT-5.4 with significant coding improvements, and living brain cells were taught to play DOOM. Also covered: new MacBook Pros with M5 Pro/Max.\",\n    \"author\": \"The Changelog\",\n    \"source\": \"Podcast\",\n    \"url\": \"https://changelog.com/podcast/605\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-05-08\",\n    \"topics\": [\"openai\", \"gpt-5.4\", \"anthropic\", \"claude\", \"aws\", \"infrastructure\", \"brain-computer-interface\"],\n    \"type\": \"podcast\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"The Changelog: Burke Holland on Opus 4.5 and AI coding\",\n    \"description\": \"Burke Holland from GitHub Copilot discusses how Opus 4.5 changed everything in AI coding, the 2x usage bump from Claude, and GPT-5.3 Codex living up to the hype. Deep dive into practical AI coding workflows.\",\n    \"author\": \"The Changelog\",\n    \"source\": \"Podcast\",\n    \"url\": \"https://changelog.com/podcast/604\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-05-08\",\n    \"topics\": [\"ai\", \"coding\", \"github-copilot\", \"anthropic\", \"claude\", \"openai\", \"gpt-5.3\", \"gpt-5.4\", \"developer-experience\"],\n    \"type\": \"podcast\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"Using Claude Code: The Unreasonable Effectiveness of HTML\",\n    \"description\": \"Thariq Shihipar (Claude Code team) advocates for HTML over Markdown as LLM output format. HTML enables SVG diagrams, interactive widgets, in-page navigation, and richer explanations. Simon tested this by having GPT-5.5 create an HTML explanation of the copy.fail Linux security exploit, producing rich, interactive documentation.\",\n    \"author\": \"Simon Willison (citing Thariq Shihipar)\",\n    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/May/8/html/\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-05-08\",\n    \"topics\": [\"llm\", \"prompt-engineering\", \"html\", \"claude-code\", \"documentation\"],\n    \"type\": \"technical\"\n  }\n]\n",
